      "notes": [
        "Releases now include small TUI-only downloads for Linux x86_64, Apple silicon macOS, and Windows x86_64 alongside the full desktop bundles. These archives contain no Qt runtime; the macOS download is signed and notarized.",
        "The terminal process tree now matches the desktop focus and order-lock behavior. Press `f` or `Shift+Enter` to focus the selected subtree. Keyboard, scrolling, and overlay interaction hold row order through the next telemetry sample and a short settling delay. Metrics still refresh in place, and the header shows when reordering is paused.",
        "Hoddmimis now has a keyboard-complete terminal interface. Run `hoddmimis-tui` on Linux and macOS or `hoddmimis-tui.exe` on Windows; Linux and macOS desktop installations also accept `hoddmimis --tui`. The dedicated command does not require Qt or a display server. It shares process identity, settings, snapshots, privacy rules, inspections, and process-action safety with the desktop app. Use `--ascii --color never --no-mouse` for conservative or remote terminals, and press `?` for the in-app key reference.",
        "Windows x86_64 is now a supported desktop target. The portable ZIP includes Qt and is checked by a packaged offscreen launch before publication. Live Windows process rows include CPU, memory, executable, account, handle, and thread data plus identity-safe actions. GPU, per-process network, icons, and detailed inspector queries remain unavailable on Windows."
      ]
    },
